    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d686">

                <pb facs="0734" n="622" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg622"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/4164: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Poole</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-03-29T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 29, 1919,
                                5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>565. Reply from Secretary of State to your telegram number 48, to Mission
                    February 27th, 5 P.M.,<anchor n="22" xml:id="d686-f1"/> second paragraph, reads
                    as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Navy’s action will closely conform to policy concerning Northern Russia
                            which Government decided to follow. The Navy is sending one gunboat, one
                            cruiser and three torpedo boats and is holding certain smaller vessels
                            for use in case of need. Navy does not contemplate any further action
                            unless developments or change of policy indicate necessity
                            therefor.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Department understands six submarine chasers may also be ordered to Murmansk.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d686-f1" n="22" xml:id="d686-f1-content">
                <p>Same telegram as that to the Secretary of State, no. 908, Feb. 27, <ref
                        target="#pg618">p. 618</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
